        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-105917",
        ":question/problem": "The rate at which a liquid cools is proportional to the difference between its temperature and the temperature of its surroundings. Let $T(t)$ be the temperature of the liquid in degrees Celsius, and let $t > 0$ be the time in minutes. If the temperature of the surroundings is $25^{\u2218}C$, which differential equation could be used to model the temperature of the liquid? Assume that $k > 0$ is a constant of proportionality."
