        ":question/problem": "A turkey reaches ${145}^{\u2218}\\text{F}$ in the oven. After removing the turkey from the oven, the turkey's temperature $T(t)$ decreases at a rate that obeys Newton's law of cooling. Here, $T$ is measured in degrees Fahrenheit, and $t>0$ is the time in minutes. If the room temperature is ${67}^{\u2218}\\text{F},$ which differential equation could be used to model the temperature of the turkey? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.",
